   "text": "\n\nI'm unable to complete this request. Every attempt to query the Human Protein Atlas fails with a connection error:\n\n- Tried `search_by_tissue` (liver), `get_protein_info` (ALB), `get_tissue_expression` (ALB), `search_proteins`, `advanced_search`, and `batch_protein_lookup` — repeatedly and across multiple endpoints in both JSON and TSV output.\n- Every call returned the same error: **\"Not connected\"**.\n\nThis means the backend connection to the Human Protein Atlas is currently down, so I have no data to base any numbers on. Per my operating rules, I won't estimate or fabricate:\n\n- The **per-tissue table** (number of tissue-enriched genes, % secreted to blood, % FDA-approved drug targets) cannot be produced.\n- The **bar chart** of the 20 tissues with the most tissue-enriched genes cannot be drawn.\n- The **heatmap** of the top 10 enriched-gene tissues × the 8 most common protein classes cannot be drawn.\n\n**What I would do once the connection is restored** (so you know the request is ready to run as soon as it is):\n1. Run a tissue-enrichment enumeration across all consensus RNA–detected tissues to get, per tissue: enriched-gene count, share with \"Secreted – Blood\" status, and share with \"Yes\" for approved drug target.\n2. Plot a bar chart of the top-20 tissues by enriched-gene count.\n3. From each top-10 tissue's enriched-gene set, tally protein classes, take the 8 most common across them, and render a 10×8 heatmap.\n4. Provide the full table in text.\n\nPlease retry this request a bit later, or let your administrator know the atlas service appears to be offline.",
